** What is this? **

cen|sù|ra: controllo esercitato da un'autorità civile o religiosa su
pubblicazioni, spettacoli, mezzi di informazione, per adeguarli ai
principi della legge, di una religione o di una dottrina morale.
(Tullio De Mauro, il dizionario della lingua italiana.)

censor [transitive verb]: to suppress or delete as objectionable.
(Merriam-Webster's Online dictionary.)

Censorship is the removal or withholding of information from the public
by a controlling group or body. (Wikipedia entry for Censorship.)

This suite of programs implements by-domain and by-IP censorship of the
Internet. It is designed to accommodate multiple blacklists from
different Italian regulatory authorities and to be easily extensible.

BIG WARNING: This project is meant to be a TOOLKIT to meet the legal
requirements of Internet censorship in Italy. IT IS NOT meant to be
used as-is or as a stand-alone all-in-one solution.
It must be adapted and customised to YOUR systems and needs.
Feel free to modify, enable and disable features as needed.


** Supported lists **

- aams     - Agenzia Dogane e Monopoli - Gambling
             https://www.adm.gov.it/portale/siti-web-inibiti-giochi
- tabacchi - Agenzia Dogane e Monopoli - Tobacco Control
             https://www.adm.gov.it/portale/siti-inibiti-tabacchi
- agcom    - Autorità per le Garanzie nelle Comunicazioni - Copyright infringement
             https://www.agcom.it/provvedimenti-a-tutela-del-diritto-d-autore
             Note: the AGCOM website is typically one year behind;
             the PEC method (see config.sh) is strongly recommended.
- cncpo    - Centro Nazionale per il Contrasto della Pedopornografia Online
             Child sexual abuse material - list NOT available to the public
             Received via encrypted PEC. See README.cncpo.
- consob   - Commissione Nazionale per le Società e la Borsa - Unauthorized trading
             https://www.consob.it/web/area-pubblica/oscuramenti
- pscaiip  - Piracy Shield, client implementation by A.I.I.P. - Copyright infringement
             Reserved for AIIP members. See README.pscaiip.
- ivass    - Istituto per la Vigilanza sulle Assicurazioni - Insurance fraud
             https://www.ivass.it
- manuale  - Self-managed list for custom entries (domains and/or IPs)


** Project structure **

The project is organized around a simple pipeline:

  censorship-get  →  update_* / parse_*  →  build-*-config  →  censorship-apply

Detailed component map: see ARCHITECTURE.md.

Main files:

  config.sh                   Central configuration (all tuneable parameters)
  censorship-cron             Main cron entry point: calls get, summary, apply
  censorship-cron-pscaiip     Dedicated cron for Piracy Shield (runs every 5 min)
  censorship-get              Downloads and parses all configured lists
  censorship-apply            Applies the lists to DNS and IP routing
  censorship-summary          Writes list statistics to the log file
  update_<list>               Per-list download and pre-processing scripts
  parse_cncpo                 Perl parser for CNCPO CSV format
  parse_aams                  Perl parser for plain-text domain lists (also used
                              by AGCOM and other plain-text sources)
  download_*.py               Python helpers for HTTP-based list downloads
  build-bind-config           Generates the named.conf fragment for BIND
  build-unbound-config        Generates the include file for Unbound
  upload-bind-config          Distributes the BIND configuration to name servers via rsync
  upload-unbound-config       Distributes the Unbound configuration to name servers via rsync
  install-routes-linux        Installs/removes null routes (RTBH) via `ip route`
  supernets.py                Aggregates IP prefixes before installing routes
  cncpo/                      Working directory and helpers for CNCPO PEC processing
  agcom-dda/                  Working directory and helpers for AGCOM PEC processing
  db.*                        BIND zone files (one per list, contain the NXDOMAIN response)
  lists/                      Runtime directory: intermediate and final list files (gitignored)
  examples/                   Reference crontab and logrotate configuration
  contrib/                    Third-party contributed tools (e.g. censura-stats)


** Requirements **

  install-routes-linux:   iproute2
  parse_aams:             Regexp::Common >= 2013031201, List::MoreUtils, File::Slurp
  parse_agcom:            Regexp::Common >= 2013031201, List::MoreUtils, File::Slurp
  parse_cncpo:            Text::CSV >= 0.32, List::MoreUtils, File::Slurp
  upload-bind-config:     rsync (local), BIND + rsync + rndc (remote)
  upload-unbound-config:  rsync (local), Unbound + rsync (remote)
  Python >= 3.0 with the following packages

On Debian/Ubuntu, install all dependencies with:

  # apt-get install python3 python3-openssl python3-requests-unixsocket \
        python3-urllib3 python3-bs4 python3-requests libfile-slurp-perl \
        rsync wget perl libregexp-common-perl liblist-moreutils-perl \
        python3-click python3-soupsieve python3-orderedattrdict \
        python3-tldextract pip curl python3-yaml python3-imaplib2 iproute2

The following packages are not available via apt and must be installed via pip:

  # pip install urlextract ua-generator
  (add --break-system-packages if required by your system)

download_ivass.py additionally requires pypdf:

  # pip install pypdf


** Quick start **

1. Read and edit config.sh carefully before running anything.

2. Run the bootstrap script once from the installation directory:

     # bash bootstrap.sh

   This creates the required empty files and directories (lists/, tmp/, gpg/).

3. Set up the cron jobs (see Cron requirements below).

4. Configure your name servers (see Name servers configuration below).

For CNCPO, follow the additional setup steps in README.cncpo.
For Piracy Shield, follow README.pscaiip.


** Cron requirements **

censorship-cron is the main script to be scheduled via cron:

  # run every 6 hours
  27  */6  * * *   root   /root/kit-censura/censorship-cron &> /dev/null

If you are using the Piracy Shield Client by AIIP, add a second job:

  # run every 5 minutes
  */5  *   * * *   root   /root/kit-censura/censorship-cron-pscaiip &> /dev/null

See examples/crontab for a ready-to-use template.


** Logging and alerting **

Logging and alerting are configured in config.sh.

The default log file path is /var/log/kit-censura.log.
A logrotate template is available in examples/kit-censura.logrotate.

Alerting sends an email via sendmail when a list download fails.
Set NOC_EMAIL in config.sh and ensure sendmail is working correctly.


** Name servers configuration **

The following include directives must be added to your name server daemon:

  # named.conf (BIND)
  include "/etc/bind/censura/named.conf";

  # unbound.conf (Unbound)
  include: "/etc/unbound/censura.conf"

The db.* zone files must be present in the directory configured as
$CONFDIR in config.sh (default: /etc/bind/censura/).

The list of target name servers is configured via $SERVERS in config.sh.


** IP routing (blackholing) **

install-routes-linux installs null routes for the IP addresses contained
in the active lists, using $BLACKHOLE_NEXTHOP as the next hop.
It is intended to run on a border router or on a system from which a
dynamic routing protocol (e.g. quagga/FRR with BGP) will redistribute
the static routes.

The script replaces all existing null routes on each run, so it is
safe to call repeatedly.

When AGGREGATE_PREFIX=true (default), supernets.py is called first to
aggregate contiguous prefixes into the smallest set of covering CIDRs
up to the length defined by AGGREGATION_MAXLEN (default: /25).


